cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use bricksentry in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "bricksentry"
abstract: >-
  bricksentry is an open-source change-safety layer for Databricks. It helps
  data teams and AI agents understand the impact of a data change before it
  reaches production: it previews the change on a Delta shallow clone, diffs
  the data against a pinned table version, reads Unity Catalog lineage to find
  what depends on the table, applies policy rules to return a pass, warn,
  needs_human or block verdict, and prepares the RESTORE command to undo it.
authors:
  - name: "Brahma"
version: "0.1.33"
date-released: "2026-11-23"
license: Apache-2.0
url: "https://bricksentry.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bricksentry/bricksentry"
keywords:
  - databricks
  - data-engineering
  - data-quality
  - data-diff
  - delta-lake
  - unity-catalog
  - ai-agents
  - mcp
  - change-safety
